I
Abstract
The construction industry is considered to be one of the most dangerous industries
due to its wide variety of accidents and high risks. Although people have been promoting
construction safety through various means, the frequent occurrence of construction
accidents still plagues the development of this industry. As an important pillar industry of
the national economy, the transportation industry plays a vital role in the process of my
country’s modernization development. To promote the development of the transportation
industry in a more developed direction, it is indispensable to carry out bridge
construction and tunnel construction. Due to the complexity of geological conditions in
China, safety construction accidents are prone to occur during the construction of bridges
and tunnels, causing a large number of casualties and economic and property losses.
Standardization is a series of standards formulated by enterprises in order to obtain the
best production and operation order and economic benefits. It has an important guiding
and standardizing role for enterprises to carry out safe construction, and can effectively
prevent construction accidents.
In order to reduce the occurrence of bridge and tunnel construction accidents and
analyze the role and impact of standardization on reducing bridge and tunnel construction
accidents, this thesis divides bridge and tunnel construction accidents into four levels
according to the degree of casualties and economic losses. According to the linear
relationship between property losses at various levels, the quantification is used as a
weight index for network research, and a bridge construction risk network and a tunnel
construction risk network are established respectively to analyze the impact of accident
levels on risk nodes in the network. At the same time, through the common risk nodes
existing in the two risk networks, they are combined into a bridge and tunnel
construction risk network. And then use the four overall indicators of network diameter,
network density, average path length, and clustering coefficient to analyze the network
characteristics, and conclude that the bridge and tunnel construction risk network has
small-world and scale-free network characteristics. Using the two network analysis
indicators of degree and betweenness to reveal the key risk nodes of the bridge and
tunnel construction risk network, and compared with the bridge construction risk
network and the tunnel construction risk network, it is concluded that compared with
other types of risks, human factors not only induce construction accidents more


