frequently, but also cause a large number of casualties and property losses, which must
be paid enough attention by managers. At the same time, compared with the unweighted
risk network, the risk node in the bridge and tunnel construction risk network in this
study can not only reflect the frequency of other risks induced by it, but also reflect the
loss caused by the node. The larger the risk node is, the greater the property loss and
casualty will be caused by the risk, and the managers should control and defend against
these risks. On this basis, this thesis comprehensively understands and promotes the
safety of bridge and tunnel construction by accurately grasping the similarities and
differences between the causes of bridge and tunnel construction accidents and the
complex relationship between analysis standards and bridge and tunnel construction risks.
This thesis uses the citation relationship between bridge and tunnel standards
collected to build a bridge and tunnel standard citation network to prepare for the later
research on the relationship between standards and risks. On this basis, this thesis firstly
searches the standard text of the construction risk of bridge and tunnel, and uses the
reference relationship of the standard to the construction risk of bridge and tunnel, the
bridge and tunnel construction risk network and the bridge and tunnel standard reference
network are coupled into a standard-risk double-layer network, and the overall
characteristic index and node characteristic index are selected to analyze it. Based on the
original indicators, this thesis constructs four node indicators of coverage, attention,
coverage, and attention, and the overall analysis indicator of risk coverage by standards
to analyze the restrictive effect of research standards on risk, provide suggestions for the
formulation and modification of standards for enterprises to achieve the goal of safe
construction. Through analysis and research, the following problems are found in the
existing standards: the standard does not cover enough risks and fails to mention
common construction risks; the standard mentions less frequency and frequency of key
construction risks, and cannot form a good guiding role; the standard covers insufficient
types of risks, which is somewhat different from the actual situation. By revising and
formulating the standards, preparing for the improvement of the standards from multiple
levels is conducive to restraining the original risks and reducing the occurrence of
accidents. And it is helpful to put forward targeted suggestions, reduce the number of
high-frequency accident types in the bridge and tunnel industry, and better realize safety
management.
Key Words: Safety management; Social network analysis; Bridge and tunnel
construction; Accident level; Bridge and tunnel standards.


